Error [jet.AppFeatureNotOnTarget]: App feature `.draggable` needs target `native`, but the resolved target is `Wasm`.
  --> Tests/UI/app_device_bare_import_target.jet:7:16
    |
  7 | run: fn() { _: draggable(ui.text("Fix the gate"), 7, "Fix the gate") }
    |                ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A page's drag is the browser's own, and the page runtime can't carry the app's values in it yet, so the web output has no `app.draggable` to run; dropping the move would lose it.
 Fix: On the web, offer the move as buttons in the screen, one for each place the value can go. Keep `app.draggable` for a native build.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-APP-TARGET-FEATURE
